    the offline rule (decided 2026-11-05, done): "once loaded online, usable offline. never generated offline." the app pings GET /api/health at start (2.5 s, and the registry's pubkey must be ours). online: everything, and loading a vault file also asks POST /api/check and records the answer in ~/.local/share/chaos/activated.json (that is the activation; `--import` does it too). offline: no previews, no rerolls, no tickets, no `--seed` of anything not activated here. allowed: loading an activated vault file, wallpaper mode on an activated seed. the panel shows ONLINE / OFFLINE, the roll tab says why. `--dev-offline` lifts it for development. honest note: this is client code, so it is policy for honest users, not a wall. the walls are the registry's: rationed tickets, commit-reveal, one claim per seed, server-side rarity. the full flows are in "Data and logic flow"

    the file is a receipt, the website is the truth. the app never decides ownership

    google login in the app: pkce flow, system browser, refresh token in libsecret. openid email profile only, no drive scope (the old plan used drive, dropped, the website is the sync)

    sync on start, on login, on a button: send the seed_fulls you hold, get state per seed back, mark transferred / revoked locally.

    how it landed (v1.0): no oauth inside the app. the site's /login?app=1 signs you in with google and shows the session jwt; the app takes it (`--login-token`, or paste in the account tab, "open the sign-in page" does xdg-open) and keeps it in ~/.config/chaos/session (0600). libsecret later, maybe. the token rides as a bearer header on /api/me, /api/ticket, /api/claim, /api/vault, /api/sync, /api/file/:seed (client/src/sync/api.cpp, libcurl + nlohmann). `--login-dev NAME` for registries with ALLOW_FAKE_LOGIN

        `--roll`: commit, ticket, seed in one go (client/src/sync/session_flow.cpp rollClaimable). the app checks the ticket's signature and that it carries the commit it sent before trusting it. panel: one button when connected

        `--claim f.chaos` / "claim this roll": POST, verify what comes back against our pubkey and the seed, store it over the rolled file, activate it. the by-hand --commit / --ticket / --reveal path still exists for people without a session

        `--sync` / "sync vault": every non-preview seed you hold -> /api/sync -> activation updated (current or transferred away). then /api/vault: anything the registry says is yours that you do not hold (acquired on the web) is fetched from /api/file, verified, stored, activated. tested: a seed sold on the web turned STALE on the seller's app and appeared in the buyer's vault on their next sync

    instance_id: 16 random bytes made once, ~/.config/chaos/instance. goes in every .chaos so the server can ban one install if it leaks tickets (done, v0.4)

